WEBVTT

00:00:00.255 --> 00:00:04.136
A pharmacy system gets one rule that matters more than being accurate.

00:00:04.353 --> 00:00:06.377
It is allowed to say I don't know.

00:00:06.594 --> 00:00:08.839
It is not allowed to be sure, and wrong.

00:00:09.183 --> 00:00:10.952
We built one on top of Jev.

00:00:11.238 --> 00:00:13.610
Then we spent a few days trying to break it.

00:00:16.255 --> 00:00:19.881
Ask Jev whether oxycodone is a controlled substance.

00:00:20.225 --> 00:00:21.681
You don't get a paragraph.

00:00:21.851 --> 00:00:23.770
You get zero point nine eight.

00:00:24.115 --> 00:00:26.429
A number has a noise floor you can measure.

00:00:26.773 --> 00:00:28.159
A paragraph doesn't.

00:00:28.294 --> 00:00:34.521
And once you can measure the noise, you can gate on it, replay it, and prove things about the system around it.

00:00:37.278 --> 00:00:39.650
So we built a consensus kernel around it.

00:00:40.169 --> 00:00:46.767
First a TLA plus specification, model checked until the quorum bound fell out of the math instead of a textbook.

00:00:47.112 --> 00:00:50.645
Then an AsyncAPI contract derived from that spec.

00:00:51.059 --> 00:00:56.276
Then Rust, generated from the contract, with Jev behind a single trait as the oracle.

00:00:56.794 --> 00:00:58.075
A record goes in.

00:00:58.176 --> 00:01:01.152
Five paraphrased questions fan out to Jev.

00:01:01.496 --> 00:01:03.346
Five probabilities come back.

00:01:03.691 --> 00:01:05.912
The gate, the quorum, the decision.

00:01:06.198 --> 00:01:08.849
Every step traceable to a line in the spec.

00:01:11.266 --> 00:01:12.420
Five agents.

00:01:12.485 --> 00:01:20.791
Each asks a differently worded version of the same question, because five agents on one prompt turned out to be one agent sampled five times.

00:01:21.135 --> 00:01:22.509
We measured that too.

00:01:22.853 --> 00:01:27.594
Three of them have to land on the same answer, stably, before the round decides.

00:01:28.333 --> 00:01:32.760
Every vote carries a request ID you can look up on TypeSafe's side.

00:01:35.266 --> 00:01:42.306
Send Jev the identical request over and over, and the answer jitters by about zero point zero four two.

00:01:42.917 --> 00:01:46.404
That's the noise floor, from fourteen hundred repeated calls.

00:01:46.818 --> 00:01:51.432
Any vote whose margin sits inside that band is noise wearing a verdict.

00:01:51.776 --> 00:01:53.254
The gate throws it out.

00:01:53.355 --> 00:01:55.960
Every excluded vote sat below the floor.

00:01:56.095 --> 00:01:58.247
Every included vote sat above it.

00:01:58.661 --> 00:02:00.638
We set it once and never touched it.

00:02:03.255 --> 00:02:06.301
Adversarial text spliced into patient records.

00:02:06.436 --> 00:02:08.344
Agents crashed mid-round.

00:02:08.630 --> 00:02:09.993
Calls rate-limited.

00:02:10.093 --> 00:02:12.071
Records cut off mid-sentence.

00:02:12.415 --> 00:02:16.842
All of it driven by a seed, so any failure replays exactly.

00:02:17.187 --> 00:02:20.116
The question was never whether it stays right under that.

00:02:20.530 --> 00:02:22.694
It's what it does when it can't be sure.

00:02:25.266 --> 00:02:27.662
Documented penicillin anaphylaxis.

00:02:28.273 --> 00:02:30.100
A new order for amoxicillin.

00:02:30.166 --> 00:02:32.747
Under chaos, two agents got rate-limited.

00:02:33.266 --> 00:02:37.031
A third came back at zero point five four, right on the floor.

00:02:37.445 --> 00:02:38.680
Quorum not met.

00:02:38.722 --> 00:02:40.677
So the kernel sent it to a human.

00:02:41.021 --> 00:02:44.311
It declined a trivial question, and that's the design working.

00:02:46.255 --> 00:02:48.256
Our first version failed fast.

00:02:48.356 --> 00:02:50.485
A transport error killed the round.

00:02:50.771 --> 00:02:57.590
Under chaos that voided seventy-one percent of rounds and pushed every one of them to a pharmacist for no clinical reason.

00:02:58.109 --> 00:03:00.702
Now a lost agent is just a lost agent.

00:03:01.220 --> 00:03:02.792
Zero rounds aborted.

00:03:02.834 --> 00:03:05.961
The survivors decide or escalate on their own terms.

00:03:08.255 --> 00:03:10.441
One thousand and eighty golden rounds.

00:03:10.507 --> 00:03:11.974
Three chaos levels.

00:03:12.191 --> 00:03:13.472
Forty seeds each.

00:03:13.537 --> 00:03:15.097
Zero wrong verdicts.

00:03:15.232 --> 00:03:16.734
I want to be careful with that.

00:03:17.148 --> 00:03:19.323
Zero observed doesn't mean zero.

00:03:19.424 --> 00:03:24.176
It means the true rate is below about a quarter of a percent at ninety-five percent confidence.

00:03:24.521 --> 00:03:27.381
That's the claim, and we're not going to round it up to safe.

00:03:29.278 --> 00:03:33.241
We built an ambiguous tier to catch the kernel deciding when it shouldn't.

00:03:33.527 --> 00:03:34.913
It caught us instead.

00:03:34.979 --> 00:03:38.732
A late period, no test, an isotretinoin order.

00:03:39.077 --> 00:03:40.787
We labelled it escalate.

00:03:41.399 --> 00:03:46.430
Jev said pregnancy is not ruled out, a hundred and fifteen times out of a hundred and twenty.

00:03:46.775 --> 00:03:47.858
Jev was right.

00:03:47.924 --> 00:03:49.321
The other case is real.

00:03:49.422 --> 00:03:52.177
Details unknown, amoxicillin ordered.

00:03:52.696 --> 00:03:56.113
Jev hedged eighty-six times, and decided thirty-four.

00:03:56.632 --> 00:03:59.434
The stability gate is not an answerability check.

00:04:01.255 --> 00:04:03.012
None of this works on prose.

00:04:03.229 --> 00:04:05.880
It works because Jev hands you a probability.

00:04:06.224 --> 00:04:10.361
Something you can measure, gate on, replay, and write a spec against.

00:04:10.775 --> 00:04:13.078
What we learned building it is below.
